From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: appDisplay: Order apps that match a search equally by their IDs

Shell.AppSystem.search() gives the apps that match a query equally well
in one group, in the order GLib's desktop file index has them, which is
unspecified: g_desktop_app_info_search() says the inner lists have no
set order. The provider sorted each group by usage alone, so apps used
as much - every app, on a fresh session - kept that order, and it
changed between sessions: searching "se" showed Firefox before Google
Chrome after one boot and after it after the next.

Break the tie by the apps' IDs, so equal results come in the same order
at every search.

--- a/js/ui/appDisplay.js
+++ b/js/ui/appDisplay.js
@@ -1822,8 +1822,11 @@ export class AppSearchProvider {
                 const app = this._appSys.lookup_app(appID);
                 return app && this._parentalControlsManager.shouldShowApp(app.app_info);
             });
+            // Apps of a group match equally well, and GLib gives them in no set
+            // order: those used as much are in their IDs' order, the same at
+            // every search.
             results = results.concat(group.sort(
-                (a, b) => usage.compare(a, b)));
+                (a, b) => usage.compare(a, b) || a.localeCompare(b)));
         });
 
         results = results.concat(this._systemActions.getMatchingActions(terms));
